{"id": "De4Iihpx14M", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Ram shot Vali from behind a tree. Was it FAIR? 🏹 Comment YES or NO 👇 | Ramayan Part 8 of 12\n\n🐒 By lake Pampa, Hanuman came to Ram dressed as a monk. Ram was amazed: not one mistake in his speech! (Kishkindha Kanda 3)\n💛 Hanuman's king Sugriva showed Ram the jewels Sita had dropped. Lakshman said: \"I don't know her earrings. But these anklets, I know. I bowed at her feet every day.\" (Kishkindha 6)\n👑 Sugriva's brother Vali had thrown him out, and taken his wife. (Kishkindha 8–10)\n🌼 Sugriva challenged Vali, but they looked so alike, Ram couldn't shoot. So Sugriva wore a garland of flowers, and fought again. (Kishkindha 12)\n🌳 From behind a tree, Ram's arrow struck Vali. (Kishkindha 16)\n⚖️ Dying, Vali asked: \"You hid and shot me. Is that dharma?\" Ram answered: \"You took your brother's wife. This land is Bharat's, and I punish wrong in his name.\" Vali accepted, and asked Ram to protect his son Angad. (Kishkindha 17–18)\n\n➡️ Part 9: Hanuman leaps the ocean! Follow @therishikatha so you don't miss it!\n\n📚 Rishi Katha picture books tell our gods' stories for kids, in simple words and bright pictures. Insta Family Sale on Books 1–3, till 25 Oct → rishikatha.com (link in bio)\n\n💬 So, was it fair? Comment YES or NO, and tell us why 👇\n🔖 Save this, and share it with someone you love debating with 😄\n\n#ramayan #ramayana #vali #sugriva #hanuman #lakshman #kishkindha #valmikiramayana #jaishriram #sanatandharma #hindumythology #indianmythology #ramayanseries #rishikatha #mythologyforkids", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1792845062, "like_count": 1855, "comment_count": 48, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1391949402929008a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 55.674, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https