"17915548554540298", "text": "Yes ,fair", "timestamp": 1793111333, "like_count": 1}, {"author": "lizaallison_108", "author_id": "63999270289", "id": "18471806098143666", "text": "Yes it's completely fair as vali already had a boon of sacking half energy of his opponent and shri Ram knew that therefore to punish the sinner he had to shot from behind a tree😊", "timestamp": 1793046808, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "someone666585", "author_id": "36782896588", "id": "18572014225072850", "text": "Shri Ram got the Karma in shri Krishn avatar, got shot from a adivasi by mistake, as both shri krishn and that adivasi was the incarnation of Shri Ram and Vali", "timestamp": 1792926328, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "_saran_vemuru_96_", "author_id": "66324986153", "id": "18159352687511753", "text": "Yes it is totally fair. And i am not going to say that everything done by God is correct but i am gonna say Shri Ram Chandra murthi did because it is dharma. Or else he would not have. This is explained by Chaganti Koteswara rao garu as  Every doable thing has it's own dharma. Assume it as rules and regulations. In this way, Shri Ram Shooting Vali from the tree comes as hunting as I said every doable thing has it's dharma hunting too does. And according to that Hunter dharma he could shoot an animal down from a distance or without it's acknowledgement. Which means What Shri Ram Chandra Murthi did was never questionable  Jai Shree Ram", "timestamp": 1792924310, "like_count": 1}, {"author": "mahi.talkies", "author_id": "77974729143", "id": "18080428163387054", "text": "also vali was given a necklace that could attain half the power of person facing him so attacking him from behind was right option", "timestamp": 1792919667, "like_count": 44}, {"author": "junnusss.pmn", "author_id": "48022747919", "id": "18129050200887768", "text": "2 negatives CAN make a positive!", "timestamp": 1792895603, "like_count": 1}, {"author": "atokplanetballs", "author_id": "70108845186", "id": "17970840372159557", "text": "Jesus Christ is only true God Amen makes some stories on Jesus too ❤️🙌😢 Other are just myths Jesus is real and Jesus have proofs of existence", "timestamp": 1792863833, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "the_infamous_rudra", "author_id": "53072087441", "id": "18635457274016992", "text": "So everyon talking about the karma that ram faced when he was reincarnated as Krishna. That was due to Gandhari's curse not related to this incident. This even is completely fair bcuz Vali was an animal. As a human ram was within dharma when he hid behind a tree and shot Vali (Bcuz we hunt animals by hiding behind a tree). So yeah hope this helps and Trying to correct people", "timestamp": 1792859163, "like_count": 3}, {"author": "apuxhu", "author_id": "74833635846", "id": "18126107686916268", "text": "It wasn't fair. But Vali's boon made him impossible to defeat head on (gets half of his opponents strength in a duel). Ram received his karma in the next reincarnation in Lord Krishna's form in the end of Mahabharata. After Gandhari's curse his clan was destroyed in an internal feud (they killed themselves just like how her sons killed themselves) , Lord Krishna left Dwarka and was resting under a tree when a hunter mistook him for a deer and shot his foot with an arrow. He passed away. Pandavas learn of this, and they exit their kingdom and start their final journey towards the Himalayas, before that they perform the final rites of Lord Krishna. Krishna's heart didn't burn in the cremation as it was overflowing with divine energy. So the pandav placed it in a river stream.. letting it get carried away by the river current.. It finally reached Puri, where the King amazed by this heart, placed it in an idol and built the legendary temple of Jagannath.. the heart is now called \"bramha padarth\" and the idol is replaced every few years where the head priest holds this divine matter blindfolded and places it in a new idol. The whole Puri is in black out during this replacement process.", "timestamp": 1792855335, "like_count": 8}, {"author": "__rijuquu", "author_id": "49686901983", "id": "17966585199216623", "text": "Every deed has its karma as well. Even Shri Krishna accepted his death at the hands of Jara, who was Vali in his previous life. Just as Ram shot Vali with an arrow by hiding, Jara did the same, but this time unintentionally.", "timestamp": 1792855178, "like_count": 7}, {"author": "aight_bet6", "author_id": "15370073898", "id": "17994931380058638", "text": "Awesome 🔥❤️", "timestamp": 1792854821, "like_count": 1}], "webpage_url": "https://www.instagram.com/p/De4Iihpx14M/", "webpage_url_basename": "De4Iihpx14M", "webpage_url_domain": "instagram.com", "extractor": "Instagram", "extractor_key": "Instagram", "thumbnail": "https://instagram.fblr2-3.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t51.82787-15/861236740_18128811205755882_3518693138817952094_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_e15_tt6&_nc_cat=107&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&ig_cache_key=NDAxNDk5NjYyNDc2OTUwNjgyOA%3D%3D.3-ccb7-5&ccb=7-5&_nc_sid=58cdad&efg=eyJ2ZW5jb2RlX3RhZyI6IkNMSVBTLnhwaWRzLjEwODAuc2RyLnZpZGVvX2RlZmF1bHRfY292ZXJfZnJhbWUuQzMifQ%3D%3D&_nc_ohc=Ox51YDHE-hoQ7kNvwGZylBk&_nc_oc=AdoZIT6WaUWNjUw3QFCGPjxns66waxeHiEN-HVRLTD_w4VBG953qgteEAVk8KhDB1iKrnd5yRGCEHteWI76Ti2kY&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=instagram.fblr2-3.fna&_nc_gid=YpDtPDwCs4gHsfQin17G0A&_nc_ss=70689&oh=00_AQQpXkX44rmaHLJYCDob2pCbfEoHKV9MvGyijSd8OxRhow&oe=6AF7EE98", "display_id": "De4Iihpx14M", "fulltitle": "Video by therishikatha", "upload_date": "20261024", "epoch": 1794256762, "format": "dash-1391949896262292v - 1080x1920 (DASH video)+dash-1391949402929008a - audio only (DASH audio)", "format_id": "dash-1391949896262292v+dash-1391949402929008a", "ext": "mp4", "protocol": "https+https", "format_note": "DASH video+DASH audio", "tbr": 2895.608, "width": 1080, "height": 1920, "resolution": "1080x1920", "dynamic_range": "SDR", "vcodec": "vp09.00.40.08.00.02.02.05.00", "vbr": 2839.934, "aspect_ratio": 0.56, "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "abr": 55.674, "asr": 48000, "_type": 